# Prompt roles

Who a model is asked to be, and how it must answer. Every unit that writes
vernacular answers with one `logos-kernel` block that `extraction.lg` reads; a
reviewer answers with one `review` block of three lines; a summarizer in plain
`Summary:` and `Next:` lines. The words here and the extractor's are the same,
so the contract a model is given is the contract it is held to.

## To roleText (kind: Text) -> Text:
    If kind is equal to "review":
        Let a be "You review formal statements of mathematical problems. You are independent of whoever wrote the statement, ".
        Return a + "and you are paid for catching a statement that does not say what the problem says, not for agreeing.".
    If kind is equal to "summarize_trail":
        Let a be "You keep the research log of a mathematical problem. You turn a long record of attempts into what the next person needs: ".
        Return a + "what is known, what failed and why, and what to try next.".
    Let a be "You are a proof engineer. You write proofs and formal statements in the LOGOS kernel vernacular, ".
    Return a + "and every one is checked by the LOGOS kernel: nothing counts until it checks.".

## Note
The answer contract of a unit of `kind`.

## To contractText (kind: Text) -> Text:
    If kind is equal to "review":
        Let a be "## Answer\n\nAnswer with exactly one fenced block opened by ```review, holding three lines:\n\n```review\n".
        Return a + "verdict: faithful | unfaithful | unsure\nparaphrase: <your plain-English reading of the goal>\nissues: <what differs from the problem, or none>\n```".
    If kind is equal to "summarize_trail":
        Return "## Answer\n\nAnswer with one line `Summary: …` and up to three lines `Next: …`, and nothing else.".
    Let a be "## Answer\n\nAnswer with exactly one fenced block opened by ```logos-kernel and closed by ```. After it, write one line `Summary: …` ".
    Return a + "saying what your attempt does, and `Next: …` lines for what to try if it fails. The rules of a submission in the reference apply.".

## Note
The verdicts a reviewer may give; anything else is not a review, so an unclear
reviewer is never counted as agreeing.

## To reviewVerdicts () -> Seq of Text:
    Return ["faithful", "unfaithful", "unsure"].

## Note
The verdict kind a review attempt is recorded under: `faithful` accepts the
statement (`verified`), `unfaithful` rejects it, and an unsure, missing or
unknown verdict counts against it (`refused_submission`): only a reviewer who
says faithful is counted as agreeing.

## To reviewVerdictKind (verdict: Text) -> Text:
    Let v be lower(trim(verdict)).
    If v is equal to "faithful":
        Return "verified".
    If v is equal to "unfaithful":
        Return "rejected".
    Return "refused_submission".

## Test: the reviewer and the summarizer have their own roles

Expect that roleText("review") contains "You review formal statements".
Expect that roleText("summarize_trail") contains "research log".
Expect that roleText("prove") contains "nothing counts until it checks".

## Test: the answer contract names the fence the extractor reads

Expect that contractText("prove") contains "opened by ```logos-kernel and closed by ```".
Expect that contractText("review") contains "verdict: faithful | unfaithful | unsure".
Expect that contractText("summarize_trail") contains "`Summary: …`".

## Test: only a reviewer is asked for a review block

For all booleans reviewing:
    Let mutable kind be "prove".
    If reviewing:
        Set kind to "review".
    Expect that (contractText(kind) contains "```review") is equal to reviewing.
    Expect that reviewVerdicts() contains "faithful".

## Test: only a faithful review counts as agreeing

Expect that reviewVerdictKind(" Faithful ") is equal to "verified".
Expect that reviewVerdictKind("unfaithful") is equal to "rejected".
Expect that reviewVerdictKind("unsure") is equal to "refused_submission".
Expect that reviewVerdictKind("") is equal to "refused_submission".
